 ## [Unreleased]
 
 ### Added
+- **Exit option in the tray menu.** Right-click the tray icon > **Exit PhraseLock** closes the background monitor and, if Auto-protection is on, its watchdog first so nothing restarts it. It asks for confirmation, and for the emergency password (3 tries) when one is set, so it cannot be used to dodge the lock. New `exit_app.py` and the `--exit-monitor` argument.
 - **Emergency unlock wording per pack.** A pack's `ui_texts` can now set the emergency dialog's texts (`emergency_open`, `emergency_title`, `emergency_prompt`, `emergency_submit`, `emergency_back`, `emergency_continue`, `emergency_wrong`) and its "are you sure?" screens (`emergency_steps`: up to 5 `{title, text}`, used position by position, the rest keeps the built-in wording). TechDom (Vex, admin override) and PetDom (Juno's spare key) ship their own. Packs you save from your settings carry them too.
 - **Safer emergency unlock.** Before the emergency password is asked, the lock screen now shows 1 to 5 "are you sure?" screens (3 by default), each with a 3-second wait and a button to go back and type the phrase instead. Optional penalty once the emergency password is used: reset the current streak (the best streak is kept) and/or lose some XP. Both are in *Settings > Protection > Emergency override* and described on the last screen. New settings `emergency_confirmations`, `emergency_penalty_streak`, `emergency_penalty_xp` (not changed by theme packs); new `emergency.py`.
 - **Uninstall and cleanup button.** *Settings > Protection > Uninstall and clean up...* asks what to remove (stop PhraseLock and its watchdog, the start-with-Windows shortcut, your settings/stats/packs/logs in `%APPDATA%\PhraseLock`, and the `PhraseLock.exe` file itself), shows a summary and only acts after you confirm. The emergency password is required when one is set. New `uninstall.py`.
